EXPERIMENT-3: Parallel Sum using OpenMP (C++)
=============================================

REQUIREMENT:
- g++ compiler must be installed
- On Windows: Install MinGW-w64 from https://www.mingw-w64.org/
  During install, select Architecture: x86_64 and add it to PATH
- Check if installed: g++ --version

Steps to Run:

1. Compile the C++ program:
   g++ -fopenmp distributed_sum.cpp -o sum.exe

   ERROR: 'g++' is not recognized?
   >> g++ is not installed or not in PATH.
   >> Install MinGW and restart your terminal after installation.

   ERROR: fopenmp: No such file?
   >> Your g++ version does not support OpenMP.
   >> Reinstall MinGW-w64 (the 64-bit version includes OpenMP by default).

2. Run the compiled program:
   On Windows:  .\sum.exe
   On Linux/Mac: ./sum.exe

   ERROR: sum.exe is not recognized?
   >> Use .\sum.exe (with dot-backslash) on Windows PowerShell.

   >> The program will ask: Enter number of elements (N)
   >> Then: Enter elements (type numbers separated by Enter)
   >> It will show each thread's partial sum and the final total.

NOTE: The number of threads used depends on your CPU cores.
NOTE: Output order of threads may vary each run — that is normal.
